9
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Demented is a 2000 black comedy film written and directed by John Waters.

10
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:46,000
The film stars Melanie Griffith as a snobby A-list Hollywood actress who is kidnapped by a
band of terrorist filmmakers; they force her to star in their underground film.

11
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:56,000
Stephen Dorff stars as the eponymous character and leader of the group, with Alicia Witt, Adrian Grenier,
Maggie Gyllenhaal, and Michael Shannon co-starring as the rest of his gang of filmmakers.

12
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
The film, whose title (also the name of Dorff's
character) alludes to director Cecil B.

13
01:07:10,000 --> 01:07:16,000
DeMille, is loosely based on the 1974 kidnapping of
Patricia Hearst, who has a cameo role.

14
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:26,000
Like all of Waters' films, it was shot in Baltimore, Maryland.

15
01:17:30,000 --> 01:17:36,000
The film was given a limited theatrical release in the United
States on August 11, 2000, by Artisan Entertainment.

16
01:22:40,000 --> 01:22:46,000
The film explores themes of biological weapon, zombie, lethal
virus, struggle for survival, group of friends.

17
01:27:50,000 --> 01:27:56,000
The tone is dark.
